-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 16 07:45:00 UTC 2026 - Nicolas Morey <nicolas.morey@suse.com>

- Release 2.0
  - Switch to unified CRED_ENV v1 hybrid envelope encryption
    (RSA-OAEP-SHA256 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM) with per-file random
    keys and eliminate the shared <hostname>.key file
  - Bind the CRED_ENV v1 header, relative FUSE path, and POSIX file
    permissions (st_mode & 07777) into AES-256-GCM Additional
    Authenticated Data (AAD) to prevent ciphertext substitution and
    chmod tampering
  - Derive plaintext file size directly from the CRED_ENV v1 header and
    drop the user.size extended attribute requirement
  - Add cred-encrypt and cred-decrypt CLI utilities
  - Verify TPM public key attributes, pin the TPM object Name across
    decryptions, and add the tpm_pubkey mount option
  - Harden TCTI validation: scrub TSS2/TCTI environment variables,
    require /dev/tpmrm[0-9]+ for device TCTI, and restrict swtpm TCTI
    to test builds

